\title{attest: check whether RNA-seq count data can support the analysis run on it}
\description{
\code{attest} audits a count matrix, its sample sheet and its design before
differential expression. It does not analyse expression. Each check
adjudicates one claim and returns a verdict - \code{PERMITTED}, \code{CAUTION},
\verb{NOT PERMITTED} or \code{UNKNOWN} - with the evidence behind it and the checks the
inputs could not answer. \code{UNKNOWN} always means "the inputs cannot answer
this", never a guess, and nothing throws: malformed input returns a typed
result with a reason.
}
\details{
Start with \code{\link[=attest]{attest()}} on a matrix, \code{SummarizedExperiment}, \code{DESeqDataSet} or
